# Build context is the repo root now that one image builds both halves.
#
# Without this, `COPY frontend/ ./` in the build stage copies the HOST's
# frontend/node_modules straight over the one `npm ci` just produced in
# the image -- linking the build against whatever binaries happen to be
# on the developer's machine. Non-reproducible builds, and a plausible
# cause of "the fix didn't show up after redeploying".
**/node_modules

# Build output. Never an input.
frontend/dist
frontend/dist.*

# Vite writes a config timestamp file per dev-server start; dozens
# accumulate and there is no reason for any to enter the image.
frontend/vite.config.js.timestamp-*.mjs

# Python bytecode and test/lint caches. The image compiles its own.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
backend/.pytest_cache
backend/.ruff_cache

# The live database and TLS material live on named volumes, never baked
# into the image.
backend/data
data
tls

.git
.gitignore
.github
.trash
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store

# Documentation is not a build input. PROJECT-PLAN.md alone is >500 KB.
*.md
